      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, the model is not assuming inherent instability in the cultural or religious structures themselves. Rather, \"environmental complexity\" refers to the sheer number of variables and interpersonal dynamics present in large, communal settings compared to an individual's controlled routine. Highs and lows in such social networks can lead to unpredictable life events—like sudden large family emergencies or varying exposure levels—which translates to higher long-term unpredictability in the underwriting context.",
      "source": "target",
